    "model_design": "Implement multi-sample dropout by replacing the single forward pass with K=4 forward passes through the classifier_head in the model's forward method, averaging the resulting logits before returning. Specifically, in forward(), compute 4 independent output tensors by iterating through the classifier_head 4 times on the same input, average them, and return the averaged logits. This does not change the model architecture or the MultiPoolingHead class, only the forward loop. This directly addresses overfitting by introducing stochasticity during training without modifying the loss function or requiring separate dropout masks. The backbone remains unchanged. This change is applied only during training; during inference, use a single forward pass (K=1) by setting a flag or simply not iterating.",
    "training_evaluation": "Change the learning rate for the head from 3e-5 to 2e-5, increase warmup_ratio from 0.1 to 0.3, set GRADIENT_ACCUMULATION_STEPS to 1, increase BATCH_SIZE to 24, and reduce MAX_LENGTH to 192. These adjustments are applied in the CONFIGURATION and during optimizer/scheduler initialization. The longer warmup and lower LR allow the optimizer to explore more carefully in the overfitting-prone regime, and the larger batch with less accumulation provides more stable gradients. The shorter sequence length respects the dataset's short average sentence length and reduces memory, enabling the larger batch. All other training settings (EMA decay 0.995, FGM epsilon 0.5, progressive unfreezing stages, early stopping patience, weight decay, gradient clipping, DataLoader num_workers, pin_memory) remain unchanged as per the initial plan's 'keep unchanged' list."
  }
